  "body": "Tying into https://github.com/heycam/webidl/pull/635 , it's important to know the current realm to define where things are coming from. The ES spec defines the \"current realm\" based on execution contexts, and it saves and restores the current realm for Promise jobs with a dummy execution context.\r\n\r\nDoes HTML have a similar mechanism for queued tasks? I'm having trouble finding it, if so. Whatever mechanism is adopted should also somehow work if the task is queued from an \"in parallel\" algorithm--maybe we should define the \"current Realm\" in parallel even if you can't allocate from there.\r\n\r\n@Ms2ger , would you be interested in this task? As \"in parallel\" and \"queue a task\" are defined in HTML, seems like this is the place to make the fix, not WebIDL, but it's all part of the same project.",
